;; db: bench_bowtie
;; BOWTIE, monolithic, adversarial spelling: same 6 atoms as
;; bowtie_mono.slog but with both CLOSING edges written last -- the shape a
;; user produces by listing "the path" first and "the checks" at the end.
;; A data-blind schedule that follows source order expands
;; X->Y->M->U->V (a 4-path) before either triangle check prunes anything.
table (edge int int)
table (bt int int int int int)

rule (edge X Y) (edge Y M) (edge M U) (edge U V) (edge X M) (edge M V) --> (bt X Y M U V)
